# Self-documentation wave for the dev-agents repo
# Sequential: README first, then operator guide (no same-file conflicts)

1 | docs-writer | Update the dev-agents README.md so it accurately documents multi-vendor CLI orchestration as of mid-2026. Fix the intro that still says the toolkit mainly works with Claude Code only — state clearly that agents run via claude, kimi, and grok CLIs with zero API keys. Add a clear Operator quickstart section covering: (1) co-pilot chat in any CLI vs fleet dispatch from the shell; (2) plan file format WAVE agent task branch with a warning that raw pipe characters inside task text break parsing and that VERDICT lines must use slashes not pipes; (3) how to run dispatch.sh with git SSH repo URL, Homebrew bash, --auto and --retries; (4) workers.yaml provider_preferences (web-frontend primary kimi) and routing.yaml provider_failover; (5) make scorecard; (6) worker login notes (claude, kimi, grok login) and that non-interactive ssh needs Claude credentials reachable outside Keychain only if already documented in learnings — do not invent secrets. Keep Paperclip sections accurate but secondary. Link to docs/plan-file-format.md and providers READMEs. Acceptance: README is coherent for a new operator, multi-vendor is front-and-center, no broken relative links you introduce, commit and push branch, open a draft PR if gh is authenticated else note that. Write handoff.md at repo root before exit. | feat/docs-readme-multi-vendor

2 | docs-writer | Add a new operator guide at docs/operator-guide.md for the dev-agents fleet. Cover end-to-end: when to stay in a single CLI vs when to use dispatch; writing a plan under wave-plans/; autoplan.sh optional review; dispatch.sh invocation; watching logs; handoff ledger Phase 1 locations under wave-plans wave handoffs (jsonl mechanical + md intent) and that Phases 2-5 of the shared brain are parked after A/B; [blind] marker for critic control tasks; common failures (HTTPS clone auth, branch already exists fixed by checkout path, plan pipe delimiter, gh 401). Include a short cookbook with copy-paste examples. Link from README if README already has an operator section, otherwise only create this file. Acceptance: file exists, is accurate against scripts/dispatch.sh and scripts/run-remote.sh behavior, commit and push, draft PR if possible. Write handoff.md before exit. | feat/docs-operator-guide

3 | docs-writer | Update docs/plan-file-format.md with hard rules learned in production: (1) branch is the last field and should look like feat/slash-slug; (2) never put unescaped pipe characters inside the task description — use PASS / REVISE / BLOCK not pipe-separated verdicts; (3) producer then critic must be different waves when they share a branch; (4) optional note that critic tasks reviewing an existing branch rely on run-remote checking out that branch. Keep the existing format table. Acceptance: doc updated, no contradiction with README, commit push, draft PR if possible. Write handoff.md before exit. | feat/docs-plan-format-hard-rules
